WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:07.915
Meridian has new funding to bring clean water to the health centres in Kilifi.

2
00:00:07.915 --> 00:00:12.750
Nadia, the M&E officer, sets the project up before any data comes in.

3
00:00:13.171 --> 00:00:16.475
She starts a new project under the Healthy Start programme.

4
00:00:25.629 --> 00:00:28.593
Two years, from October, with its approved budget.

5
00:00:35.309 --> 00:00:36.853
Joseph will manage it.

6
00:00:36.853 --> 00:00:38.397
She saves the project.

7
00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:42.571
Now the results framework,

8
00:00:42.571 --> 00:00:46.183
the chain from what the project does to the change it should bring.

9
00:00:49.764 --> 00:00:54.134
At the top, the impact: the long-term change the work contributes to.

10
00:00:59.958 --> 00:01:01.384
Under it, the outcome.

11
00:01:01.384 --> 00:01:05.079
Health centres have safe water and handwashing every day.

12
00:01:15.649 --> 00:01:19.289
Each level says what has to hold for it to lead to the next.

13
00:01:19.289 --> 00:01:22.140
Here, that the county keeps paying for repairs.

14
00:01:22.553 --> 00:01:25.451
And the output the project delivers directly:

15
00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:28.993
staff trained in water safety and infection prevention.

16
00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:43.785
The chain reads top to bottom.

17
00:01:43.785 --> 00:01:46.918
Now each result needs an indicator to measure it.

18
00:01:47.325 --> 00:01:51.631
For the output, a count: how many health centre staff finish the training.

19
00:02:01.932 --> 00:02:06.504
It is a number, counted in people, added up across centres and quarters,

20
00:02:06.504 --> 00:02:08.218
and reported every quarter.

21
00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:15.689
Joseph is responsible for it, and every figure is split by sex,

22
00:02:15.689 --> 00:02:19.434
so the team can see whether women and men are both reached.

23
00:02:19.866 --> 00:02:21.655
She creates the indicator.

24
00:02:22.847 --> 00:02:24.667
For the outcome, a percentage:

25
00:02:24.667 --> 00:02:29.337
the share of supported health centres with safe water every day of the month.

26
00:02:39.729 --> 00:02:42.565
A percentage needs its two parts written down,

27
00:02:42.565 --> 00:02:44.970
so everyone calculates it the same way.

28
00:02:48.661 --> 00:02:50.328
Reported every quarter.

29
00:02:50.328 --> 00:02:51.416
She creates it.

30
00:02:54.523 --> 00:02:55.541
Now the targets.

31
00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:58.023
She opens the staff training indicator.

32
00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:01.057
Targets are set for each reporting period.

33
00:03:01.496 --> 00:03:06.283
For October to December, forty staff: twenty-four women and sixteen men,

34
00:03:06.283 --> 00:03:08.477
since most nurses here are women.

35
00:03:08.924 --> 00:03:10.869
And fifty for the next quarter.

36
00:03:10.869 --> 00:03:13.881
Later periods can be added once they are set up.

37
00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:23.826
The indicator page now has everything a reporter needs: the definition,

38
00:03:23.826 --> 00:03:28.012
how it is counted, who is responsible, and the targets by sex.

39
00:03:28.462 --> 00:03:31.476
Back on the framework, the whole chain is in place,

40
00:03:31.476 --> 00:03:34.312
with an indicator on each result that needs one.

41
00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:41.052
From here, she can build a form that feeds these indicators,

42
00:03:41.052 --> 00:03:44.659
and the first figures will have targets to be measured against.
